# /etc/vpn/vpn-only: things that must only work through a VPN (the kill switch).
# After editing:  vpn apply          (manual: ~/vpn-setup/MANUAL.md)
#
# One entry per line:
#   - a domain; it also covers all its subdomains        e.g. chatgpt.com
#   - an IP or IP range, for apps with built-in addresses  e.g. 91.108.4.0/22
# While no VPN is up (and the kill switch is on), these don't work at all.
# Don't list huge shared domains (google.com, googleapis.com, cloudflare.com, amazonaws.com).

# --- ChatGPT (site)
chatgpt.com
# ChatGPT also loads files from these; uncomment to cover them too.
# oaistatic.com
# oaiusercontent.com

# --- Claude Code and claude.ai (app + site)
anthropic.com
claude.ai
claude.com
